  "Question": "The points \\(A(1,y_1)\\), \\(B(2,y_2)\\), and \\(C(-3,y_3)\\) all lie on the graph of the inverse proportional function \\(y=6/x\\). What is the order of \\(y_1\\), \\(y_2\\), and \\(y_3\\)?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(y_1>y_2>y_3\\)",
    "B": "\\(y_3>y_2>y_1\\)",
    "C": "\\(y_2>y_1>y_3\\)",
    "D": "\\(y_1>y_3>y_2\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Substituting each point gives \\(y_1=6\\), \\(y_2=3\\), and \\(y_3=-2\\), so \\(y_1>y_2>y_3\\). Note that C is in the third quadrant, where \\(y\\) is negative, so it is the smallest.",
